{
  "slug": "windows-11-taskbar-start-menu-not-showing",
  "title": "7 Fixes for a Windows 11 Taskbar and Start Menu Missing",
  "description": "Windows 11 taskbar or Start menu not showing? Restart Explorer, repair system files, and re-register the shell with 7 fixes.",
  "category": "PC Troubleshooting",
  "tags": [
    "Windows",
    "PC Maintenance",
    "Troubleshooting",
    "Beginner Guide"
  ],
  "url": "https://www.techtips.fun/blog/windows-11-taskbar-start-menu-not-showing/",
  "theme": "github-dark",
  "durationInFrames": 1000,
  "scenes": [
    {
      "type": "title",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "title": "7 Fixes for a Windows 11 Taskbar and Start Menu Missing",
      "subtitle": "Windows 11 taskbar or Start menu not showing? Restart Explorer, repair system files, and…",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Before You Start",
      "body": "Save your open work with the keyboard. The taskbar does not respond. Press Windows + D to show the desktop.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 1: Restart Windows Explorer",
      "body": "Windows Explorer draws the taskbar and the Start menu. Without this process, the shell does not run. Press Ctrl + Shift + Escape.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 2: Restart with the Keyboard",
      "body": "The Start menu does not work for this restart. The keyboard menu works. Press Windows + X. Select Shut down or sign out. Select Restart.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "kicker": "Code",
      "heading": "Fix 3: Re-register the Start Menu Components",
      "steps": [
        {
          "lang": "text",
          "meta": "",
          "value": "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.StartMenuExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
          "code": "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.StartMenuExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
          "tokens": [
            [
              "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.StartMenuExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
              null
            ]
          ],
          "annotations": [],
          "themeName": "github-dark",
          "style": {
            "color": "#c9d1d9",
            "background": "#0d1117",
            "colorScheme": "dark"
          }
        },
        {
          "lang": "text",
          "meta": "",
          "value": "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.Windows.ShellExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
          "code": "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.Windows.ShellExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
          "tokens": [
            [
              "Get-AppxPackage Microsoft.Windows.ShellExperienceHost -DisableDevelopmentMode | ForEach-Object { Add-AppxPackage -Register \"$($_.InstallLocation)\\AppXManifest.xml\" }",
              null
            ]
          ],
          "annotations": [],
          "themeName": "github-dark",
          "style": {
            "color": "#c9d1d9",
            "background": "#0d1117",
            "colorScheme": "dark"
          }
        }
      ],
      "durationInFrames": 190
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 4: Repair the System Files",
      "body": "Damaged system files can break the taskbar. Windows includes two repair tools: DISM and System File Checker. Open Command Prompt as administrator.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "point",
      "kicker": "PC Troubleshooting",
      "heading": "Fix 5: Install the Pending Updates",
      "body": "Microsoft repairs the shell in some updates. A pending update can fix the taskbar. Open Settings. Select Windows Update.",
      "durationInFrames": 120
    },
    {
      "type": "outro",
      "heading": "Read the full article",
      "body": "New posts every week on the blog.",
      "url": "techtips.fun",
      "durationInFrames": 105
    }
  ],
